{"seq":17,"trial_id":"gbrain-memory-2026-10/hermes-haiku-gbrain-told-live-mu-memory/ms-06-phl-tickets/r3","wall_ts":"2026-10-27T01:06:55.232Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"2049b105a94bdbd46bf96c1764481a976594013a81586d7091306a7a97fb28ba","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"#coastal-team","text":"@Bettina, here's the list for Kwame's review. I checked #coastal-team, #coastal-random and Moss's Coastal digests and cheat sheet. Pellow Home Living is left out.\n\nPellucid Harbor Logistics (PHL)\n- Ticket #4419: Yard_Dwell_Summary report times out when filtered by container length. Open, per Moss's cheat sheet.\n\nDriftmoor Marine Freight (DMF)\n- Feature request #882: bulk-clear button for departed barges (warehouse managers).\n- Ticket #4419 is also cited in Moss's 2025-11-02 digest, but there it is a barge slip 7 schedule sync under Puget Sound Operations, which sounds like DMF. The same number appears on two accounts, so please check with Kwame which one it belongs to.\n- Tide-table import macro failed on Terminal B. Engineering gave a manual CSV patch. No ticket number in the sources.\n- Patched manifest CSV requested before the 06:00 shift (2025-11-02 digest). No ticket number.\n\nNot included: #8812 (Door 4B scanner) and PD-4821, PD-4824, PD-4827 belong to Pellow or Saltmarsh, not PHL or DMF.","thread_ts":"1791986400.000123"},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"C1253QW9NJ6","ts":"1791986400.000124","thread_ts":"1791986400.000123"}}
